Socnet - Direct blockmodeling in C#
===================================
Version 1.4 (October 2025)
Carl Nordlund - carl.nordlund@liu.se

Socnet.se was supported by NordForsk through the funding to
The Network Dynamics of Ethnic Integration, project number 105147
Nordint.net: https://nordint.net

How to cite specific methods, type in 'citeinfo()'.

Entering interactive mode (type 'quit' to quit, 'help' for help):
> Loading and executing 'deterministic_script.txt'...
> help
HELP SECTION
============
Version 1.4 (October 2025)
See website for documentation:
https://socnet.se
 
The socnet client is used to do blockmodeling analyses, with some extra functionality for data management.
You type in commands on the prompt to do various things with data: load, save, transform,  analyze etc.
Check www.socnet.se for command references, how-to, and quick-start tutorial!
> citeinfo()
The Socnet.se software client:
  Nordlund, C., Roy, C. (2024). Socnet.se: The Blockmodeling Console App [computer software]. https://socnet.se
 
Direct blockmodeling using the 'nordlund' method (i.e. weighted correlation coefficients):
  Nordlund, C. (2020). Direct blockmodeling of valued and binary networks: a dichotomization-free approach. Social Networks, 61, 128-143.
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.socnet.2019.10.004
 
Correlation-based core-periphery approach, ignoring inter-categorical blocks or using the 'denuci(d)' ideal blocks:
  Borgatti, S.P., Everett, M.G. (2000). Models of core/periphery structures. Social Networks, 21(4), 375-395.
  https://doi.org/10.1016/S0378-8733(99)00019-2
 
Correlation-based core-periphery approach using 'pco(p)' for intra-core and/or 'den(d)' or 'denmin(d)' for inter-categorical ties:
  Estévez, J.L., Nordlund, C. (2025). Revising the Borgatti-Everett core-periphery model: Inter-categorical density blocks and partially connected cores. Social Networks, 81, 31-51.
  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.socnet.2024.11.002
 
Power-relational core-periphery approach with core dominance and/or peripheral dependency (i.e. 'powerrelational' argument in 'coreperi'):
  Nordlund, C. (2018). Power-relational core–periphery structures: Peripheral dependency and core dominance in binary and valued networks. Network Science, 6(3), 348-369.
  https://doi.org/10.1017/nws.2018.15
 
Direct generalized blockmodeling using 'hamming' distances as penalty function:
  Doreian, P., Batagelj, V., Ferligoj, A. (2004). Generalized Blockmodeling. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.
  https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511584176
